From: ASRock Rack X570D4I-2T OpenBMC port
Subject: [PATCH] skip nbdkit credential args when there are no credentials
Upstream-Status: Pending

bmcweb always creates the credentials pipe and always writes username and
password, empty strings included (see 4bbf2a13c2), so the daemon's credentials
object is never null and "if (credentials)" never skips. An anonymous https://
mount therefore gets "user=" and "password=+<tempfile>" passed to nbdkit, plus
a VolatileFile created and torn down, for a server that was never going to be
asked to authenticate.

Gate on there actually being a secret rather than on the object existing.

This is a tidiness fix, not a crash fix: the SIGABRT and the resulting
"nbdkit: error: open /tmp/VM-xxxxxx: No such file or directory" that
originally motivated it are fixed by 0004, which removes the abort inside the
VolatileFile constructor. Do not credit this patch with fixing those.

diff --git a/src/state/activating_state.cpp b/src/state/activating_state.cpp
index c495653..deb625f 100644
--- a/src/state/activating_state.cpp
+++ b/src/state/activating_state.cpp
@@ -276,8 +276,16 @@ std::unique_ptr<resource::Process>
         "tls13-ciphers="
         "TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384"};
 
-    // Authenticate if needed
-    if (machine.getTarget()->credentials)
+    // Authenticate if needed.
+    //
+    // bmcweb always sends the credentials pipe, writing username and password
+    // even when the request carried neither, so a non-null credentials object
+    // does not mean there is anything to authenticate with. Sending "user="
+    // and "password=+<tempfile>" for an anonymous fetch is meaningless to the
+    // server and costs a temp file for no reason.
+    if (machine.getTarget()->credentials &&
+        !(machine.getTarget()->credentials->user().empty() &&
+          machine.getTarget()->credentials->password().empty()))
     {
         // Pack password into buffer
         utils::CredentialsProvider::SecureBuffer buff =
